1304
01:37:52,895 --> 01:37:54,994
Kayleigh...

1305
01:37:54,995 --> 01:37:56,894
Do you ever think about us?

1306
01:37:56,895 --> 01:37:59,954
I mean, do you ever wonder

1307
01:37:59,955 --> 01:38:02,754
if things might have been
different between us?

1308
01:38:02,755 --> 01:38:04,455
Sure, Evan.

1309
01:38:07,425 --> 01:38:10,015
You were the first person
I really ever cared about.

1310
01:38:11,655 --> 01:38:14,055
- I was?
- Yeah.

1311
01:38:15,395 --> 01:38:17,154
That's why when I was little,

1312
01:38:17,155 --> 01:38:18,895
I never went to live with my mother.

1313
01:38:20,055 --> 01:38:21,894
I don't get it.

1314
01:38:21,895 --> 01:38:24,194
When... When my folks split up,

1315
01:38:24,195 --> 01:38:27,294
they gave me and Tommy a choice
of who we wanted to live with.

1316
01:38:27,295 --> 01:38:30,054
And I couldn't stand my dad.

1317
01:38:30,055 --> 01:38:33,194
But I knew that if I went
to move with my mom,

1318
01:38:33,195 --> 01:38:35,794
I'd never see you again.

1319
01:38:35,795 --> 01:38:37,495
I didn't know that.

1320
01:38:39,195 --> 01:38:42,454
So you still think about us...

1321
01:38:42,455 --> 01:38:43,955
together?

1322
01:38:45,855 --> 01:38:49,424
Well, it's crossed my mind
from time to time.

1323
01:38:49,425 --> 01:38:51,154
And?

1324
01:38:51,155 --> 01:38:54,454
Well, a lot of things
have crossed my mind, Ev.

1325
01:38:54,455 --> 01:38:58,954
I mean, I could play out the entire
movie of our lives in one second.

1326
01:38:58,955 --> 01:39:00,994
Boom, we fall in love.
We get married.

1327
01:39:00,995 --> 01:39:04,894
We have kids.
Our kids grow old, as do we.

1328
01:39:04,895 --> 01:39:07,425
Matching burial plots.
The whole thing.

1329
01:39:08,955 --> 01:39:11,855
Plah, it took a lot longer
to spit out than to imagine.

1330
01:39:13,995 --> 01:39:16,295
Things like that usually do.

1331
01:39:18,555 --> 01:39:20,394
So...

1332
01:39:20,395 --> 01:39:22,454
Do you think that
it might have worked?

1333
01:39:22,455 --> 01:39:24,555
Yeah.

1334
01:39:26,625 --> 01:39:28,735
I mean, but that's not
how things wound up.

1335
01:39:31,195 --> 01:39:33,195
I'm with Lenny.

1336
01:39:34,425 --> 01:39:36,554
Lenny is your friend

1337
01:39:36,555 --> 01:39:38,924
and...

1338
01:39:38,925 --> 01:39:40,595
and that's where it ends.

1339
01:39:43,455 --> 01:39:45,255
Well...

1340
01:39:46,495 --> 01:39:48,894
Would it make a difference

1341
01:39:48,895 --> 01:39:50,724
if I told you that

1342
01:39:50,725 --> 01:39:52,854
no one could possibly ever love anyone

1343
01:39:52,855 --> 01:39:54,455
as much as I love you?

1344
01:40:02,595 --> 01:40:06,154
I'm not saying that. I...

1345
01:40:06,155 --> 01:40:09,794
- Yeah.
- I'm not... I'm just saying it like

1346
01:40:09,795 --> 01:40:12,924
if you were a girl,
would that be something

1347
01:40:12,925 --> 01:40:14,755
that you would want to hear?

1348
01:40:18,555 --> 01:40:20,594
Hold on one second. Lenny's calling.

1349
01:40:20,595 --> 01:40:22,525
I'll be right back, Ev, okay?

1350
01:40:28,725 --> 01:40:30,695
He's a little down...

1351
01:40:31,755 --> 01:40:33,495
I love you.

1352
01:41:29,995 --> 01:41:32,105
You forgot to put
the toaster on the ledge.

1353
01:41:33,395 --> 01:41:37,124
Lenny likes pop tarts.

1354
01:41:37,125 --> 01:41:38,825
You guys are all that matter now.

1355
01:41:41,325 --> 01:41:44,124
Man, I know it's hard,
but you can't give up.

1356
01:41:44,125 --> 01:41:47,094
I can't even fucking kill myself.

1357
01:41:47,095 --> 01:41:48,895
Don't talk like that.

1358
01:41:58,555 --> 01:42:01,354
All right, I've got
to get you out of here.

1359
01:42:01,355 --> 01:42:03,225
Visiting hours are almost over.

1360
01:42:07,425 --> 01:42:09,455
Did mom get transferred again?

1361
01:42:09,955 --> 01:42:11,524
What are you talking about?

1362
01:42:11,525 --> 01:42:13,395
She's been here the entire time.

1363
01:42:21,555 --> 01:42:25,195
Looking... good, kiddo.

1364
01:42:33,495 --> 01:42:36,324
Lung cancer?

1365
01:42:36,325 --> 01:42:39,654
You started chain smoking
when I blew myself up.

1366
01:42:39,655 --> 01:42:42,524
Sorry, Mrs. T, he's been acting
out of sorts lately.

1367
01:42:42,525 --> 01:42:44,294
I think I could fix this.

1368
01:42:44,295 --> 01:42:45,694
Fix?

1369
01:42:45,695 --> 01:42:48,655
I just need the journal entry
about the blockbuster.

1370
01:42:51,055 --> 01:42:53,894
Shit, no arms.

1371
01:42:53,895 --> 01:42:55,854
I never wrote it.

1372
01:42:55,855 --> 01:42:59,924
You're... acting... different.

1373
01:42:59,925 --> 01:43:03,124
No, he's just going through
tough times right now.

1374
01:43:03,125 --> 01:43:05,054
Mom...

1375
01:43:05,055 --> 01:43:06,954
You're going to be okay.

1376
01:43:06,955 --> 01:43:08,724
I can change it.

1377
01:43:08,725 --> 01:43:10,995
Um, maybe... I wanna go down
to the chapel.

1378
01:43:12,125 --> 01:43:16,924
You're... acting...

1379
01:43:16,925 --> 01:43:20,454
just like your father.

1380
01:43:20,455 --> 01:43:24,054
Just 'cause he went crazy
when he was my age,

1381
01:43:24,055 --> 01:43:26,525
doesn't mean
I'm gonna go crazy, mom.

1382
01:43:27,855 --> 01:43:31,554
How... did...

1383
01:43:31,555 --> 01:43:34,454
you... know that?

1384
01:43:34,455 --> 01:43:37,024
You told me...

1385
01:43:37,025 --> 01:43:39,095
on Parent's Weekend, remember?

1386
01:43:43,095 --> 01:43:45,225
It wasn't me...

1387
01:43:46,355 --> 01:43:48,624
- Just...
- ...or you.

1388
01:43:48,625 --> 01:43:51,824
like... Jason.

1389
01:43:51,825 --> 01:43:53,624
You don't worry, mom,

1390
01:43:53,625 --> 01:43:56,524
I'm going to get you
out of here. Okay?

1391
01:43:56,525 --> 01:43:58,354
No.

1392
01:43:58,355 --> 01:44:00,124
You're not going to hurt anymore.

1393
01:44:00,125 --> 01:44:02,154
I'm going to fix it.

1394
01:44:02,155 --> 01:44:03,205
No.

1395
01:44:04,695 --> 01:44:06,755
No, no.

1396
01:44:08,336 --> 01:44:11,454
Are you sure you even packed it?

1397
01:44:11,455 --> 01:44:13,294
My mom packed it.

1398
01:44:13,295 --> 01:44:15,454
I think she sent
everything I ever owned.

1399
01:44:15,455 --> 01:44:17,654
- Is this it?
- Yeah.

1400
01:44:17,655 --> 01:44:19,824
What do you want it for?
I don't get you lately.

1401
01:44:19,825 --> 01:44:21,355
Duly noted.

1402
01:44:22,756 --> 01:44:26,454
Okay, I have to ask you
one last favor.

1403
01:44:26,455 --> 01:44:28,594
- What?
- I need you to be quiet.

1404
01:44:28,595 --> 01:44:31,524
I have to concentrate if I wanna
destroy the blockbuster.

1405
01:44:31,525 --> 01:44:34,094
What?
What, the blockbuster?

1406
01:44:34,095 --> 01:44:35,754
If I hadn't blown off my arms,

1407
01:44:35,755 --> 01:44:38,654
my mom would've never
started smoking in the first place.

1408
01:44:38,655 --> 01:44:40,525
Never mind. Just open it.

1409
01:44:42,695 --> 01:44:44,624
Turn it.

1410
01:44:44,625 --> 01:44:46,225
There.

1411
01:44:50,525 --> 01:44:52,694
"Today mommy is taking me to play

1412
01:44:52,695 --> 01:44:54,594
with Kayleigh and Tommy.

1413
01:44:54,595 --> 01:44:57,925
I will meet their father and see
what a real dad is like."

1414
01:45:01,055 --> 01:45:03,425
Now, how do I destroy the blockbuster?

1415
01:45:18,655 --> 01:45:22,155
Evan, what are you doing
with that knife?

1416
01:45:25,595 --> 01:45:29,755
Well, that didn't work.
Go on, turn it.

1417
01:45:30,995 --> 01:45:32,525
Turn it. There.

1418
01:45:34,195 --> 01:45:36,894
"I never wanted
to be in the movie anyway.

1419
01:45:36,895 --> 01:45:39,454
And it was cold so
I wanted to wear my clothes.

1420
01:45:39,455 --> 01:45:41,524
But Mr. Miller made me
take my shirt off."

1421
01:45:41,525 --> 01:45:43,354
In this part of the story,

1422
01:45:43,355 --> 01:45:47,054
Robin Hood has just married
maid Marian.

1423
01:45:47,055 --> 01:45:50,624
And they have to kiss and stuff,

1424
01:45:50,625 --> 01:45:52,254
like grown-ups do.

1425
01:45:52,255 --> 01:45:54,255
Wait, I need my belt.

1426
01:46:01,195 --> 01:46:04,094
Hey, don't even bother about a belt.

1427
01:46:04,095 --> 01:46:07,754
- Hey.
- Back off, fuckbag.

1428
01:46:07,755 --> 01:46:10,894
Amazing that word never fails
to make an impression with you.

1429
01:46:10,895 --> 01:46:13,454
Easy does it, Evan.

1430
01:46:13,455 --> 01:46:16,824
Don't be a bad boy
or I'll tell your mother

1431
01:46:16,825 --> 01:46:18,724
what a naughty little shit you are.

1432
01:46:18,725 --> 01:46:20,854
And I'll tell
Child Protective Services

1433
01:46:20,855 --> 01:46:22,954
about your little
kiddie porn endeavors.

1434
01:46:22,955 --> 01:46:25,194
One step closer and I'll
shove this up your ass.

1435
01:46:25,195 --> 01:46:28,985
- Hey, that's dangerous. You could blow off your hand.
- Been there, done that.

1436
01:46:32,225 --> 01:46:33,395
Hey!

1437
01:46:37,395 --> 01:46:39,454
- Sparkler.
- Kayleigh, no!

1438
01:46:39,455 --> 01:46:42,095
No!
Kayleigh, no!

1439
01:46:49,925 --> 01:46:51,195
Hey, man.

1440
01:46:53,395 --> 01:46:55,494
...good, kiddo.

1441
01:46:55,495 --> 01:46:58,524
I've got no choice but to commit you
to Sunnyvale institution...

1442
01:46:58,525 --> 01:47:00,994
Evan, you're gonna have to live
somewhere else for a while.

1443
01:47:00,995 --> 01:47:03,794
- A squashed butterfly.
- I'm so sick of this!

1444
01:47:03,795 --> 01:47:05,794
I want my mommy.

1445
01:47:05,795 --> 01:47:08,085
I think we should
up your medication.

1446
01:47:35,855 --> 01:47:37,794
Where are my goddamn books?

1447
01:47:37,795 --> 01:47:40,954
Hey, Evan, we're not supposed
to meet for another hour.

1448
01:47:40,955 --> 01:47:43,354
Where are my goddamn books?

1449
01:47:43,355 --> 01:47:44,825
Books?

1450
01:47:46,395 --> 01:47:48,024
My journals.

1451
01:47:48,025 --> 01:47:50,054
I... I need them.

1452
01:47:50,055 --> 01:47:54,124
So, if you'd give 'em to me,
it'd help a lot.

1453
01:47:54,125 --> 01:47:56,295
It really hurts me
to go through this again.

1454
01:47:57,455 --> 01:47:59,454
There are no journals.

1455
01:47:59,455 --> 01:48:01,594
There never were.

1456
01:48:01,595 --> 01:48:04,424
It's part of the fantasy world
that your mind created

1457
01:48:04,425 --> 01:48:07,894
to cope with the guilt
of killing Kayleigh Miller.

1458
01:48:07,895 --> 01:48:10,994
Think, Evan, think.

1459
01:48:10,995 --> 01:48:13,455
You've created a disease
that does not exist...

1460
01:48:14,595 --> 01:48:16,794
alternate universes with colleges

1461
01:48:16,795 --> 01:48:19,224
and prisons and paraplegia.

1462
01:48:19,225 --> 01:48:22,254
I want my journals and I want 'em now!

1463
01:48:22,255 --> 01:48:25,294
And I know that you got 'em
and you're gonna give 'em to me!

1464
01:48:25,295 --> 01:48:27,765
You're not going to hide them
from me. I want them!

1465
01:48:29,595 --> 01:48:32,194
You're reminding me of your father.

1466
01:48:32,195 --> 01:48:34,524
He was always screaming
for a photo album

1467
01:48:34,525 --> 01:48:36,495
even though he never had one.

1468
01:48:38,095 --> 01:48:39,795
I'm so sorry.

1469
01:48:43,625 --> 01:48:45,954
A photo album?

1470
01:48:45,955 --> 01:48:47,294
Photos.

1471
01:48:47,295 --> 01:48:48,825
Evan?

1472
01:48:50,795 --> 01:48:54,055
The hemorrhaging...
The damage is irreparable.

1473
01:48:59,455 --> 01:49:02,755
Frankly, I'm surprised he still
has use of his motor functions.

1474
01:49:12,895 --> 01:49:15,354
Mom?

1475
01:49:15,355 --> 01:49:18,624
Um, did you remember to bring

1476
01:49:18,625 --> 01:49:20,755
those home movies
that we used to make?

1477
01:49:21,855 --> 01:49:23,695
Yeah, they're right here.

1478
01:49:25,225 --> 01:49:29,295
Good, because I really like
to watch them.

1479
01:49:33,155 --> 01:49:34,695
So that's good.

1480
01:49:36,746 --> 01:49:42,094
I think it's best we
transfer him to Bellevue

1481
01:49:42,095 --> 01:49:43,595
first thing in the morning.

1482
01:50:26,095 --> 01:50:29,254
"If anyone finds this,

1483
01:50:29,255 --> 01:50:33,954
it means that my plan didn't work

1484
01:50:33,955 --> 01:50:36,325
and I'm already dead."

1485
01:50:36,636 --> 01:50:40,454
He's not in his room.
Search the grounds.

1486
01:50:40,455 --> 01:50:41,094
Evan!? Over here!

1487
01:50:41,095 --> 01:50:44,324
"If I can somehow
go back

1488
01:50:44,325 --> 01:50:46,824
to the beginning
of all of this

1489
01:50:46,825 --> 01:50:51,525
I might be able to save her."

1490
01:51:03,725 --> 01:51:06,355
Jason, cut it out.
I'm trying to have a baby.

1491
01:51:17,555 --> 01:51:18,655
Go away.

1492
01:51:33,455 --> 01:51:35,154
Something's wrong!

1493
01:51:35,155 --> 01:51:36,795
It's killing me!

1494
01:51:38,825 --> 01:51:41,524
Make it stop! Oh!

1495
01:51:41,525 --> 01:51:43,494
Heart rate is decelerating.

1496
01:51:43,495 --> 01:51:45,654
What's happening?!

1497
01:51:45,655 --> 01:51:48,024
You have no lifeline, no soul.

1498
01:51:48,025 --> 01:51:49,494
You were never meant to be.

1499
01:51:49,495 --> 01:51:51,024
He's choking himself!

1500
01:51:51,025 --> 01:51:52,794
No!

1501
01:51:52,795 --> 01:51:55,224
Okay, let's do a rapid
sequence intubation

1502
01:51:55,225 --> 01:51:56,894
for C-section!

1503
01:51:56,895 --> 01:51:58,794
Save him!

1504
01:51:58,795 --> 01:52:00,454
Not getting enough oxygen!

1505
01:52:00,455 --> 01:52:03,594
- We're losing him, we're losing him!
- No!

1506
01:52:03,595 --> 01:52:05,724
Before you were born,

1507
01:52:05,725 --> 01:52:08,354
I was pregnant three times,

1508
01:52:08,355 --> 01:52:10,724
but they were all stillbirths.

1509
01:52:10,725 --> 01:52:13,995
I kind of thought of you
as my miracle baby ever since.

1510
01:52:15,055 --> 01:52:17,694
Not again!

1511
01:52:17,695 --> 01:52:20,755
No!

1512
01:52:22,395 --> 01:52:24,894
I couldn't stand my dad,

1513
01:52:24,895 --> 01:52:28,994
but I knew that if I went
to live with my mom,

1514
01:52:28,995 --> 01:52:31,555
I would never see you again.

1515
01:52:55,505 --> 01:52:58,324
I'll never let you guys
out of my sight again.

1516
01:52:58,325 --> 01:53:00,655
Kayleigh and Tommy!

1517
01:53:03,295 --> 01:53:04,795
I missed you!

1518
01:53:20,455 --> 01:53:23,255
Yeah!

1519
01:53:24,566 --> 01:53:29,194
True happiness can only be
achieved through sacrifice.

1520
01:53:29,195 --> 01:53:31,754
...like the sacrifices
our parents have made.

1521
01:53:31,755 --> 01:53:35,904
- ...for us to be here today.
- Whoo-Hoo! Great! Tommy!

